<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Theme" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a theme in e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Topic" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasTopic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e' and an entity e if and only if e is a topic in e'" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Waypoint" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/hasWaypoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a particular p if and only if p is a waypoint in e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Affected In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a thing t and an eventuality e if and only t is affected by a thing - the agent - in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The victim is affected in a killing, the cake is affected in an eating, the car is affected in the repair, the house is affected in an alteration" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A given thing can be both agent and affected in the same eventuality: for example, a person washing themselves is both agent and the affected thing in a washing; in a handshake greeting, both persons are both agents (since they are shaking the other person's hand) and affected (since their own hand is being shaken)" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAffectedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has an affected thing also has some agent" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Thing> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Agent In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a thing t and an eventuality e if and only if t acts or causes changes in some thing in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The killer is the agent in a killing, the mechanic is the agent in the repair of the car, Joe is the agent in Joe's walking, the baker is the agent in the making of the bread" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A given thing can be both agent and patient in the same eventuality: for example, a person washing themselves is both agent and patient in a washing; in a handshake greeting, both persons are both agents (since they are shaking the other person's hand) and patient (since their own hand is being shaken)" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An agent doesn't need to be a person, a living being or some other object that we would intuitively consider 'animated' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isAgentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An eventuality can have an agent without having patients or products: for example, Joe's walking has Joe has agent, but no patient or product" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Beneficiary In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p benefits from what happens in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "People with cancer are the beneficiaries in a donation to cancer research, a household is the beneficiaty in an allocation of subsidies for energy upgrades work to a company" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In some cases, the beneficiary of an eventuality is the same as the affected participant: for example, the beneficiary of a successful medication, therapy, or surgical operation is the affected participant" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isBeneficiaryIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The beneficiary is often going to be the recipient too, but there are exceptions; consider a case in which a household is awarded a grant for the energy upgrade of their house, and the grant is paid to an energy upgrade company: in that scenario, the company is the recipient of the grant, but the household is the beneficiary" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Cause Of" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two eventualities e and e' if and only if the occurrence of e contributes to make e' occur" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A simple, informal test for assessing whether an eventuality e is cause of another eventuality e' is to ask whether e'occurs (also) because of e, or whether the occurrence of e' is explained (among the other things) by the occurrence of e; if the answer is affirmative, then e entertains loze:isCauseOf with e' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCauseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Multiple eventualities can entertain the relation loze:isCauseOf with a given eventuality, since an eventuality can have more than one cause" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Component In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p composes some other particular in the context of c" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my body is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Composite Group In" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Membership> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a group g and a membership m if and only if g has some member in the context of m" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeGroupIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the membership of France in the European Union, France is the member and the European Union is the composite group; in the membership of Toyota in JAMA (Japanese Automobile Manufacturers Association), Toyota is the member and JAMA is the composite group" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Composite In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and a composition c if and only if p has as component some other particular in the context of c" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isCompositeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In my arm being part of my body, my arm is the component and my body is the composite; in a heap of sand having an individual grain as part, the heap is the composite and the grain is the component; in the composition of water by hydrogen, water is the composite and hydrogen is the component" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/ConcreteParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Concretization Of" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a concrete particular c and a schematic particular s if and only if (1) c exemplifies or has the main features of s, and (2) s provides the benchmark or the norm for the properties and the behaviour of c" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The concretizations of War and Peace are its copies, the concretizations of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 are its performances, the concretizations of Sachertorte are the individual Sachertorte, the concretizations of a software are its installed copies, the concretizations of the Toyota Corolla (as a car model) are its manufactured units" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Concretization enables schematic particulars to be located vicariously, by being located where their concretizations are; in general, a schematic particular is wholly present wherever one of its concretizations is present; since it can have multiple concretizations at the same time, a schematic particular can be located in multiple places at the same time" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isConcretizationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The concretizations of a schematic particular can deviate from it in various respects: for example, most performances of Beethoven's Symphony No 9 typically lasts between 65 and 75 minutes, but the 2018 performance from the Philarmonia Orchestra conducted by Benjamin Zander only lasts 58 minutes; in some cases, the deviation is merely an anomaly, but in other cases it entails that the concretization is defective, faulty, or bad, like a poorly made Sachertorte, or a faulty Toyota Corolla unit" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Content In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only p is enclosed or contained by some other particular in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The liquid is the content in its containment by a tank, the fluid is the content when flowing in a duct" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Destination In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the terminal point of movement or change in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The arrival point in a travel, the distribution point in a utility supply, the buyer in a property conveyance" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The change in question does not need to be a movement, but it can be a qualitative or quantitative change too: for example, if an eventuality consists in one object becoming more similar to another one, the latter will be the destination" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDestinationIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The destination does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Determination Of" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a schematic particular x and another schematic particular y if and only if x has all the essential properties of y together with further essential properties that y lacks" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Toyota Corolla Hatchback is a determination of the Toyota Corolla; the 1869 version of War and Peace is a determination of War and Peace; Apocalypse Now Redux is a determination of Apocalypse Now; heavy water is a determination of water; anthracite is a determination of coal; carbon-14 is a determination of carbon" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "If x is a concretization of y and y is a determination of z, then x is also a concretization of z; one unit of the Toyota Corolla hatchback is also a unit of the Toyota Corolla; a heavy water molecule is a water molecule; and so on" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isDeterminationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Informally, determination consists in the gradual increase in detailing and specificity of a schematic particular; it can be viewed as the schematic particulars' counterpart of subclasshood" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Earlier Than Period" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isEarlierThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a period of time p and another period of time p' if and only if p is entirely anterior to p' along the temporal axis" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Held In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e is controlled by or subordinated to some other entity in the context of e' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHeldIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The possessed thing is the held in a possession or ownership; the managed employee is the held in a management relationship" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Holder In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e controls or is super-ordinated to some other entity in the context of e' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHolderIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "the person or organisation is the holder in a possession or ownership; the manager is the holder in a management relationship with the managed employee" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Host In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p encloses, accommodates or contains some other particular in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the host in a residency or occupation, the tank is the host in the containment of a liquid, the duct is the host in the flow of a fluid, the place is the host in a position or location" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isHostIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation does not apply to a person who is 'hosting' a party or to the 'host' of a game - who are rather agents in the respective eventualities" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Substance> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Ingredient In" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isComponentIn that obtains whenever the component is a substance that occurres in the composite in a given amount" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a cake having as ingredient 200 grams of wheat flour, wheat flour is the ingredient; in the case of a solution having as ingredient 2 litres of water, water is the ingredient" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isIngredientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Substance repetition is impractical to account for in terms of number of occurrences, since the units are too many to be counted; consequently, instead of using loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences, it is advisable to specify quantities based on units of measure" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Instruction In" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isStandardIn that obtains when the standard in question is an information artefact consisting of instructions for performing the eventuality" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The assembly manual is the instruction in the assembly of a piece of furniture, the cookbook recipe is the instruction in the preparation of a cake, the workflow documentation is the instruction in the execution of a technical process, a computer programme or software is the instruction in a computational process or programme execution" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Instrument In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p enables an agent to affects some thing in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The gun is the instrument in a killing, the hammer is the instrument in the driving of a nail, the vehicle is the instrument in a journey, a debit or credit card is the instrument in a payment" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isInstrumentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The instrument in an eventuality can also be a person: for example, the messenger is the instrument in the sending of a message" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Later Than Period" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a period of time p and another period of time p' if and only if p is entirely posterior to p' along the temporal axis" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The year 2008 is later than 1972, the early-modern period is later than classical antiquity, the XVI century is later than the XIII century" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation does not obtain in those cases in which one period is only partly posterior to another one - for example, it does not obtain between the 1800-1850 period and the 1815-1870 period" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Actor> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Member In" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Group> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an actor a and a membership m if and only if a joins the goals and/or the activities of a group in the context of that m" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isMemberIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the membership of France in the European Union, France is the member and the European Union is the composite group; in the membership of Toyota in JAMA (Japanese Automobile Manufacturers Association), Toyota is the member and JAMA is the composite group" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Origin In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular entity p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the initial point of a movement or change in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The starting point in a journey, the supply point in a utility supply, the seller in a property conveyance, the seed in a plant growth" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isOriginIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The origin does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Participant In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e' determines, modifies or qualifies e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A red apple participates in its redness; Socrates participates in his wisdom; two spouses participate in their marriage; a killer, the victim, and the gun all participate in a killing; Italy, Austria and Germany all participates in Austria being located between Italy and Germany" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Intuitively, the participants in an eventuality can be viewed as the entities that are involved in it or play some role in it" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "There are various ways in which an entity can participate in an eventuality, which are expressed by means of various sub-relations of loze:isParticipantIn" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Product In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is brought into existence by some other particular in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The house is the product in a construction work, the cake is the product in the context of baking, molecules are the products in a chemical synthesis, the zygote is the product in the fertilization of a female gamete from a male gamete" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A product does not need to be a concrete particular, but it can also be a schematic particular: for example, a document or a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the product of a writing endeavour" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isProductIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Every eventuality that has a product also has some agent" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/InformationArtefact> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Recipe In" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isInstructionIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isInstructionIn that obtains when the instructions in question prescribes the ingredient ratio and/or doses and the procedure for producing concrete particulars of a certain type or with certain features" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The cookbook doses and instructions are the recipe in the preparation of a cake, a pharmaceutical formulation is the recipe in the production of paracetamol tablets, the alloy formula together with the alloying instructions are the recipe in the manufacturing of steel slabs" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Whenever an eventuality has a recipe (loze:isRecipeIn) among its participants, it will also have a product (loze:isProductIn), which will be a concrete particular" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Recipient In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if some other particular is transferred or put under the hold of p in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The payee is the recipient in a payment, the buyer is the recipient in a property conveyance, the addressee is the recipient in a shipping, the donee is the recipient in a donation" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRecipientIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Compared to an affected thing, the recipient is impacted or controlled less directly in the context of the eventuality" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Reference Point In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is the term of reference point or the reference framework for a movement, change, or comparison in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of John being taller than Dan, Dan is the reference point; in the case of an object falling down from the top of a tower, the top of the tower is the reference point; in the case of a vehicle moving on the surface of Earth, Earth - or some Earth-based geolocation framework - is the reference point" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In ordinary talk, the reference point of a movement is often not mentioned because it's identified by default with the Earth - or some Earth-based reference framework" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The possibility of absolute motion is controversial in theoretical physics and philosophy; however, this matter is operationally irrelevant, because in practice motion can only be assessed relative to a reference framework" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isReferencePointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The scope of this thematic relation is not limited to motion, but also encompasses other types of changes as well as comparisons: for example, if an eventuality consists in an object being larger than another one, the larger object will be the theme and the other will be the reference point" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Repeated Component In" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Composition> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isComponentIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isComponentIn that obtains whenever the component is a schematic particular that is repeated in the composite in multiple occurrences" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a monomer making up a polymerous sequence, the monomer is the repeated component; in the case of water having two atoms of hydrogen, hydrogen atom is the repeated component; in the case of an engine having pistons of a certain type, the piston - construed as a schematic object - is the repeated component" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The number of repetitions is going to be specified by the associated number of occurrences (loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences)" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedComponentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "While the repeated component is always going to be a schematic particular, the composite can be either a schematic particular or a concrete particular" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/SchematicParticular> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Repeated Content In" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Containment> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isContentIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isContentIn that obtains whenever the content is a schematic particular that is repeated in the host in multiple occurrences" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In the case of a blister pack containing 10 standardised 5 mg paracetamol tablets, the 5 mg paracetamol tablet - construed as a schematic particular - is the repeated content" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A containment with a repeated component is always going to have an associated number of occurrences (loze:hasNumberOfOccurrences)" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isRepeatedContentIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "While the repeated content is always going to be a schematic particular, the host can be either a schematic particular or a concrete particular" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Object> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Setting In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an object o and an eventuality e if and only if o is the setting or context in which e is the case" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The organisation is the setting of a presidency, a living being is the setting in which an organ is vital, a wall is a partition in a house" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Only objects can be settings, since they are the only particulars that have the sort of hierarchical structure in which something can occupy a role or function" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSettingIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This thematic relation is intended for those eventualities that consist in roles, positions, or functions within a setting or an organised system; the participant that occupies the role is a theme in the eventuality" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Stage Of" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two eventualities e and e' if and only if e is a stage or phase in the occurrence of e' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The construction of the foundations of a house is a stage of the construction of the whole house, the preparation of the dough is a stage in the making of a pizza, the positioning of the explosive is a stage in the demolition of a building, the fermentation of the must is a stage in the production of wine" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Given an eventuality e and a period of time t, e can have at the most one stage that occurs from the start to the end of t" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStageOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "In other upper-level ontologies, relations like this are considered special cases of parthood, since the stages of an eventuality can be viewed as its 'temporal slices'; however, we prefer to suspend the judgment about whether the stages of an eventuality are to be considered among its parts" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Standard In" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sub-relation of loze:isTopicIn that obtains when the topic provides the rules or standard for the performance of the eventuality" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Regulations are the standard in a compliant business operation, best practices are the standard in a technical development, the workflow is the standard in the execution of a technical process" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isStandardIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Only eventualities that have humans as agents (loze:isAgentIn) or are executed by objects designed by humans - like an automated system - can have a standard (loze:isStandardIn), since treating something as a rule or standard for an action requires human-like cognitive faculties" <https://loze-ontology.org/artefacts-information-and-instructions> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Subperiod Of" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between two periods of time of which the former is a part or segment of the latter" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubperiodOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The year 1969 is a sub-period of the XX century, the period 1740-1751 is a sub-period of the period 1740-1789, the June of 1816 is a sub-period of the year 1816" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Subsequent Period To" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isLaterThanPeriod> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a period of time p and another period of time p' if and only if p immediately follows the end of p' along the temporal axis" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The XIX century is subsequent to the XVIII century, the 4th of May of 1999 is subsequent to the 3rd of May of 1999, the year 1768 is subsequent to the year 1767" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isSubsequentPeriodTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Since the 4th of May of 1999 starts when the 3rd of May ends, one could argue that there is actually an instant of time that belong to both the 3rd and the 4th; these are complex issues at the interface of metaphysics and mathematics that we cannot address here; however, their practical relevance is nil, since we will never need to refer to instants, but only to extended, non-instantaneous periods of time" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Theme In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is in a certain state or occupies a position in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In a marriage, both spouses are themes; in the case of a glass lying on a table, the glass is the theme; in the case of an amount of liquid contained in a tank, the amount of liquid is the theme; in the case of somebody owning a real estate, the real estate is theme" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isThemeIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "That of the theme is a broad thematic relations that can be useful whenever no other thematic relation applies; that being said, more specific sub-relations should be defined whenever needed" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Entity> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Topic In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an entity e and an eventuality e' if and only if e is a subject matter of cognition or meaning in the context of e' " <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Joe is the topic in an identity check, an electrical system is the topic of an electrical safety report, cancer (as a schematic particular or a class of eventualities) is the topic in a cancer research, liberty is the topic of John Stuart Mill's essay 'On Liberty', a book (in abstraction from its copies) is the topic of a review" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isTopicIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Since a cognition can be about abstractions, the topic of an eventuality can also be a class or a schematic particular" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Particular> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is Waypoint In" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://loze-ontology.org/isParticipantIn> <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between a particular p and an eventuality e if and only if p is an intermediate point of movement or change in the context of e" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An intermediate stop in a travel, the ducts linking the supply point to a distribution point" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/isWaypointIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The waypoint does not need to be a place, but it can be a thing or a period of time too" <https://loze-ontology.org/> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Materials and Composition" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze-foundation.ttl that consists of classes and relations intended for the modelling substances and material composition" <https://loze-ontology.org/materials-and-composition> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Suggested Social Extension" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze-foundation.ttl pertaining to the social domain" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Among the other things, this extension includes a minimal taxonomy of living beings, which not even remotely expected to replicate the richness and depth of a full biological taxonomy - the so-called Tree of Life; if needed, the present taxonomy could be dramatically expanded" <https://loze-ontology.org/suggested-social-extension> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Temporal Relations" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://loze-ontology.org/> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extension of loze-foundation.ttl that consists of relations for modelling temporal location, coordinates, and duration" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "throughout Time" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period t if and only if e occurs starting from the beginning of t and until the end of t" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred throughout the 1939-1945 period, the Thirty Years' War occurred throghout the 1618-1648 period, Napoleon's life occurred throughout the 1769-1821 period" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/throughoutTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The function of this relation is to specify the temporal location of an eventuality as a whole" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "until Time" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains between an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e ends at t" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/untilTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred until 1945, the Thirty Years' War occurred until 1648, Napoleon's life occurred until 1821" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://loze-ontology.org/Eventuality> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "within Time" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://loze-ontology.org/PeriodOfTime> <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relation that obtains betwen an eventuality e and a period of time t if and only if e occurs throughout a a sub-period of t" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
<https://loze-ontology.org/withinTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "WWII occurred within the XX century, the Thirty Years' War occurred within the 1620-1650 period, the Italian Renaissance occurred within the second millenium" <https://loze-ontology.org/temporal-relations> .
